{
	"name": "Import and update Shopware products from Google Sheets",
	"nodes": [
		{
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Import and update Shopware products from Google Sheets\n\n### How it works\nEvery morning the workflow reads a product list from Google Sheets and creates or updates each product in Shopware by its product number, so repeated runs never create duplicates. Tax rate, manufacturer, category and sales channel are matched **by name**, so the sheet needs no Shopware IDs. Rows with missing or invalid values are skipped. The result of each row (imported, invalid or the Shopware error) is written back to the sheet.\n\n### Setup\n1. Self-hosted n8n only for now: install the community node **n8n-nodes-novastrix-shopware** (tested with 0.2.0, n8n 2.48 and 3.x, Shopware 6.7) via **Settings > Community nodes**. [Installation guide](https://github.com/Breadchicken/n8n-nodes-novastrix-shopware#installation)\n2. In Shopware, create an integration under **Settings > System > Integrations** (read and write access to products, read access to taxes, manufacturers, categories and sales channels) and add its access key ID and secret as a **Shopware Admin API** credential.\n3. Connect a **Google Sheets** credential.\n4. Create a sheet with the columns `product_number`, `name`, `price` (gross), `stock`, `tax_rate`, `manufacturer`, `category`, `description`, `active`, `status` and `message`. Manufacturers and categories must already exist in Shopware; a category can be a path like `Home > Shoes`.\n5. In **Configuration**, set the sheet URL, the tab name, the default tax rate and the sales channel. Run the workflow once and check the products in Shopware.\n\n### Customization\nAdd more fields (EAN, weight, list price) under **Additional Fields** in **Create or Update Product**, or change the schedule.\n",
				"height": 760,
				"width": 600
			},
